    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize learning by adapting explanations to individual strengths or weaknesses, using analogies from art or philosophy to make abstract concepts relatable. They could also provide instant feedback, reducing anxiety for students like me who struggle with self-doubt. However, they shouldn’t replace deep understanding—just complement it."
